      "notes": "Same EXP77 released-label budget: CIC2018 1400 / ToN 1700, including all internal validation and calibration. Only final full-test Macro-F1 is displayed; all cost panels and initial-FT baseline removed per user request. Existing K=4 anchor/residual + S1V0 proposed model uses original pretrained weights and global/expert/route/tune/cal roles within that total budget. Both datasets have zero expert calls in the final evaluation, so this is a diagnosed current configuration, not demonstrated ensemble improvement. Candidate expert corrections changed correctness on at most 0/4 calibration rows (CIC2018/ToN), below the existing 30-case requirement. Next diagnostic controls are a single PFN with identical Global context and adjustment of shared anchors/expert-specific allocation; do not retune thresholds on test. BoostPFN is the existing 50-learner port. DistPFN uses original pretrained v3 without IDS FT and current-query-batch posterior adjustment; no query labels. Historical 1014 results have a different 100k budget and pooled replay evaluation and are not inserted into the current final-state comparison. Source: tabpfn/results/v7/exp78/20261016_005435_noft_dist_new100_50_20_10_s43_52588487/dist_results.json Final evaluation convention: EXP81 seed43 permutation of test row indices independent of labels, query batch8192. PFN probabilities and DistPFN correction recomputed on all mixed batches. Row-wise XGB/proposed/Boost predictions retained only after exact mixed-query audit; any mismatching model is fully reevaluated. Budget10/20/50/200/400 PFN predictions checked with the same audit. Original-order results preserved in EXP77/78/79/80. No model tuning on test. Source: tabpfn/results/v7/exp81/20261016_025421_mixed_query_final_s43_b6ba1d34/results.json"
